syntax "match x:\n case {'a': 1, 'a': 2}: pass" mapping pattern checks duplicate key ('a')
syntax 'match x:\n case [*a, *b]: pass' multiple starred names in sequence pattern
syntax 'match x:\n case a | b: pass' name capture 'a' makes remaining patterns unreachable
syntax 'match x:\n case {**_}: pass' invalid syntax
syntax 'match x:\n case x:\n  pass\n case 1: pass' name capture 'x' makes remaining patterns unreachable
syntax 'match x:\n case [a, a]: pass' multiple assignments to name 'a' in pattern
syntax 'match x:\n case 1 + 1: pass' imaginary number required in complex literal
